WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.880
So last time on True Fear I talked about the LA Sleepwalker.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.640
If you haven't seen that video, click here and you can go check it out.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.460
GO CHECK IT OUT!

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:19.900
So I never saw the LA Sleepwalker again, but I did make a habit of going out there to check to see if it was a habit.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.400
That he was doing it every night or something.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.560
He wasn't, but what I did notice was some other very strange things around my apartment complex.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.880
Now, this was not a nice apartment by any standards.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.400
But, it was student housing and it was close to school.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.380
I wish I had never stayed there but there's nothing I can do about it now.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.600
So anyways, there are all these closets scattered around the apartment complex,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.480
and usually they're just closed and locked,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.960
but when I got back one night from going to check for the sleepwalker,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.900
I noticed that one of them was open.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.320
And none of them have ever been open before,

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.200
so me and my roommates go to investigate, and we just find all of this crazy stuff inside of the closet.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:00.400
Lawn chairs, cones, a shovel... just all of these random objects that anyone who lives in an apartment would never really need.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.500
I don't remember all of the exact items though.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.940
And the thing that was really weird about this was that none of our resident keys gave access to any of the closets.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:12.320
So if these closets weren't for resident storage, who were they for?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:19.420
So we decided to do a little investigating and check out all the doors in the apartment complex that didn't lead to other people's units.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.860
Most of the closets were either locked or empty.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.580
But we did discover two new doors that we could access.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:26.240
One was at the end of our hallway,

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.100
which you can actually see here in Dead Air.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.660
and the other one was on the hallway opposite of ours.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.760
And they both led to these secret stairways.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:37.860
Which probably weren't a secret to the stoners of this apartment building because they both smelled like weed.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.080
The stairway closest to us had a doorway leading out to the side alley,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.440
while the one on the other side did not.

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.200
We always thought that the main staircase, which you can see right here in Acrimonious,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:50.820
was the only way to get up or down in the building, because whatever labels that had been on these stairwells

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.620
to tell you that they were stairs,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.440
had been torn off.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.040
But the most important part was at the top of each stairwell there were two doors.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.580
One leading back to the resident hallways, and one leading to... we don't know what.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.860
So we wanted to figure out what these other doors led to.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.100
At the top of the staircase closest to us, the door was locked.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.080
But on the other side, it was open.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.020
Behind the door, there's this tiny closet,

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.460
and in the back of the closet there's this metal hatch.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.780
About 2' x 2'.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.040
So we open the hatch and it leads to this chute.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.640
We look down in the chute, and there's this secret room underneath.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.320
And we had no idea how to access this room from the rest of the building.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.340
And we had no idea that it existed before.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.360
So I poked my head down there and it was pitch black,

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.440
but with the help of a phone light, we were able to see a few things.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.880
There were some boxes, some canned food, and a sleeping bag.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.740
So I immediately pulled my light out of there,

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.940
because what's going through my head is there's someone living down there,

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:41.560
and if they see the light, they're probably going to walk underneath and look back at us.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.180
And if something like that did happen,

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.160
I imagine the person would probably be enraged that we found out that they were living down there.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.340
Because, let's face it, the management to that building, however lazy they may be,

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.860
probably wouldn't be too happy if there was someone secretly living inside,

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.320
and they would be likely to investigate.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.480
Actually on second thought, that management literally didn't care about us at all..

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.920
but that would be considered trespassing if somebody was down there,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.020
so if somebody found out they could potentially get the police involved.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.560
Think about if you were living down there and somebody found out about you.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.120
That's potentially threatening your entire existence.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.340
Your entire way of living.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.100
You would probably want to do something about it.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:19.840
And I know that sounds kind of overdramatic, but you have to keep in mind that these people on the streets in LA are there for a reason.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.900
It's a sad reality, but you see a lot of people who are mentally ill, or at least mentally unstable.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:29.360
So honestly the idea of somebody seeing us and coming after us was not entirely out of the question.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.700
Especially considering the fact that we had nowhere to hide, because

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.760
they know that we live in those apartments.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.980
And they could easily follow us back or lurk by the entrance until we go in or out.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.420
And I know this whole thing might sound a little over the top

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.180
considering we had no actual evidence that anyone was living down there,

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.880
just a top-down view of some canned food and a sleeping bag,

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:54.020
but you have to remember that I have a very dark imagination and there was enough evidence to at least confirm that there was SOMETHING going on.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:58.620
So we went back to our apartment and started discussing what we had seen,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.880
and thus, the idea of The Hobo King was born.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.520
...Or at least... it started as just an idea...

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.640
Being creative people, we came up with this whole scenario and character revolving around The Hobo King.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:15.840
In our story, The Hobo King is actually a very smart man who figured out how to live his life safely and efficiently

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.300
without needing to get a job

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:21.640
and has sinced reached out to other homeless people in the area to give them a shelter overnight.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.760
So he dubbed himself The Hobo King and started donning tattered robes made up of rags

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.800
and one of those Burger King birthday crowns that he found in the dumpster.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.600
He's a very egotistical character.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.600
So over time he amassed all of these followers.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:37.820
And he gave them a place to stay in exchange for collecting taxes from the people off the streets.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:42.280
So if you're homeless, and you want to stay in The Hobo King's "castle" if you will,

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.620
you could do so by giving him 20% of the earnings that you made begging by the freeway ramp.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.520
So that's the extent of what we made up.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.260
The rest of this is all real.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.620
I'll still be referring to the homeless person as The Hobo King for the rest of the story though.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:57.720
So from that point forward, we started checking up on the closets

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.220
and monitoring what was going on on the property after the staff left every night.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.400
What we found, was that while all the closets are usually locked,

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.160
every now and then, a random one of them would be left open.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.200
And we would just find more weird things inside.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.160
But that one door at the end of the staircase that led to the chute was always open.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.940
We think that somebody left it open a while ago,

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.260
one of the staff members, and perhaps forgot about it and it's just been left open ever since.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.700
But the question still remained:

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.700
How was The Hobo King getting access to this supposedly gated property?

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.460
Who was the one getting inside and granting access to all of these doors and closets?

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.960
To answer that, we looked at the three types of people who have access to the property:

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.780
The residents, the managers, and the maintenance guy.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.140
Anyone else who came onto the property, like pest control for example,

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.760
was an independent worker and didn't have access to anything.

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.440
As I mentioned earlier, as residents, we didn't have access to any of those doors because none of our keys worked on them.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.900
So that just left the manager and the maintenance guy.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.880
Both of them were absolutely awful.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:56.240
The manager would really only stop in for about an hour every day to meet with potential leasers

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:57.580
and then leave right after that.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.380
We know this because whenever we had a problem and we tried to get ahold of the manager,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.940
it was impossible and we would end up just having to wait around all day by the manager's office.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.180
That just leaves us with the maintenance guy

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.000
who was abhorrently lazy.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:13.060
Whenever we had an issue, he would just show up like a week later with one of his friends.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:16.480
Yes, he would just bring some of his friends to work with him sometimes.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.560
We would tell him about the problem we were having,

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.520
he would be like, "oh, OK, I'll be right back,"

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.180
and then he would leave and never come back.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.700
But we did notice that he would spend a lot of time behind closed doors in his office

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.340
talking to one of his friends that he had brought to work

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.840
which led me to this theory.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.100
One of the maintenance guy's friends is The Hobo King.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.080
The maintenance guy feels bad for him,

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.020
and leaves him open a closet or room to stay in each night.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.160
After The Hobo King gains some followers,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.080
he convinces the maintenance guy to let a few of them stay as well.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.400
Over time, it leads to an infestation.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.080
This theory is backed up because during the day, when the maintenance guy was in,

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.420
is when all the locks would get changed.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.540
Which was also when we were away at class.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.940
We would also see the maintenance guy roaming around with a huge key ring

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.440
with dozens and dozens of keys.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.180
And finally, the maintenance guy was always in his office,

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:05.040
but he was never actually out maintaining or fixing anything.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.580
We continued to keep tabs on all the activity that was taking place around the apartment complex.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.980
But what we really wanted to know was how to access that secret room.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.820
With the exception of opening the hatch, throwing a rope, and climbing down.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:20.560
And then being stuck down there with a potentially crazy homeless person.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.420
And no exit.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:28.040
We assumed that the chute, and another chute that we assumed also exists on the stairwell by our side,

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:29.860
were both garbage chutes at one time

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.240
that they just got too lazy to keep taking to the street,

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.720
and then moved the dumpsters to the street for us to take our garbage out to.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.220
If that's true, then there had to be an entrance somewhere,

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.040
most likely in the two alleyways on either side of the building.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.980
First, we checked the alleyway on our side.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.460
We didn't find a secret door on our side, but we did find

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:52.660
all these SCUBA books and SCUBA equipment that had just been scattered out in the alley for some reason...

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.100
I really don't know what to make of that.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.800
That doesn't even have to do with the story at all.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.580
But I just thought I'd throw that in there.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.480
We had to hop a fence to access the alleyway on the other side.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.860
A fence that seemed to be guarding nothing but an empty alleyway.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:10.820
Until we found a door on the side of the building that lined up with the exact location where the secret room should be.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:16.240
We were actually pretty nervous to go inside, because what if there was a homeless person living in there right now?

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.420
But, we wanted answers, so we decided to just quietly go inside and see if there was anything going on in there.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.680
So I go down the alleyway to open the door.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.120
My roommates get ready to run, if need be.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.000
I turn the handle and...

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:30.080
the door's locked.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.200
But here's the thing,

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.840
we don't know if it's locked from the inside or the outside,

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.060
so just to play it safe, we book it.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:37.640
All the way back to the other side.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.280
All the way back until we're safe inside of our apartment.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:46.420
So for a while we're just sitting there discussing it and kind of building on the lore of The Hobo King.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.300
So in the apartment we have this big rear-projection TV.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:53.960
While we were talking, I kept looking over at the window because I felt like I saw something moving.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:57.100
And I should add that the window leads to the alleyway on our side.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:00.060
And then at one point I thought I saw something on the TV.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:01.320
But the TV was off.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.040
This was a reflection.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.340
And in the reflection, I see the outline of a man's head staring through the window.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:09.640
I look over to the window and the man's gone.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:14.200
I look back to the TV to see if it was maybe something else, and whatever it was, was gone.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.720
All I can see in the reflection is the empty window.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.300
Now I'm not going to immediately cry Hobo King, because we did make that character up,

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:26.580
but I don't think it's out of the question to suggest that there may have been someone living in the building.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.420
Or maybe not.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.480
I mean, we had a neighbor who lived next to us, who had somebody break in through his window.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.380
So it really could have been anybody.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.960
But there is one more chapter to this story.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:39.040
We didn't end up staying at the apartment complex much longer than that.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.100
And no, we did not leave because of The Hobo King,

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.060
but basically what happened is there was this leak in our ceiling,

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:47.100
and the maintenance guy was too lazy to fix it,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.880
and it turned into a hole in the ceiling,

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.280
and once the hole formed in the ceiling we got bed bugs,

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.380
and it was just this whole huge disaster.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.460
The bed bugs were a fate far worse than any Hobo King.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.680
Or really far worse than anything at all.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:09:59.820
It was an awful experience.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.300
But that's a whole nother story.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.060
But anyways, we were kind of getting over the whole Hobo King thing,

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.060
because we hadn't seen anything in a while,

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:12.520
but before we left, we were walking around and noticed that there was one more closet door that had been left open.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.980
And it wasn't one that we had previously seen open at any time before.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.100
So we opened it.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:21.340
There were some electrical panels, wires and switches, a potted plant...

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.620
But on the floor...

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.160
There was a blanket and pillow.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:28.080
And it wasn't like they were folded up and stored in the corner,

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.260
they were laid out like an actual bed.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:35.340
But the craziest part of any of this, was in the closet there was a bunch a graffiti on the walls.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:40.100
And they were mostly just like, "so and so was here," and pictures of penises and what have you,

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.680
but there was this one little bit of text that completely blew my mind.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.660
It said: King.

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:53.300
So as we were filming this, my buddy WestDakota, who's helping me film these videos,

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:58.360
actually mentioned that he has a little bit more information that I wasn't even aware of,

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.000
so I'm gonna hand it over to him.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.680
So this apartment complex ended the contract with our school due to a whole slew of issues,

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:09.760
but a couple months before that contract ended, hanging up around the complex were signs

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:13.200
telling the residents to make sure that the gates were closed

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:16.300
because there were a bunch of homeless people getting into the complex

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:18.940
and sleeping in the closets you've been told about,

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:24.700
so that just confirms the story a little bit more about how there were homeless people staying in this apartment complex.

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.840
And I didn't even know that going into this.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.380
I just asked Dakota to come to help me make a video.

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:31.040
He didn't know that I was recording this at all,

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.320
and he'd just happened to stumble upon that little bit of information.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:38.280
This was the last of what I have to tell about The Hobo King.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:43.000
I was actually working on a found footage web-series for a while based on our apartment complex and

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.580
our idea of what The Hobo King might be.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:49.960
It included characters that represented each of us, as well as some new made up characters.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:53.800
Sadly I never got to shoot it before the bed bugs forced us out of that place

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:58.260
and the script really did rely on the geographical layout of that complex.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.340
However...

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:03.800
After the bed bugs, we found ourselves hopping around from hotel to hotel for a while.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:09.540
So on the next episode of True Fear, I'll be telling you guys about the crazy woman in one of the rooms.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.040
There's a crazy woman in one of the rooms!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.980
Leave your own theories about The Hobo King in the comments.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:20.300
If we get 200 likes on this video, I will read you guys the script for my found-footage web-series about The Hobo King

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:24.080
Either here, or on my other series, Al Dente Creepypasta,

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:27.420
so make sure to share this video, get it out there, get it some likes,

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.700
and as always don't forget to subscribe and I will see you in the next video.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.740
Assuming we both survive.

